<html><body style='font-family:Arial, sans-serif'><h1 style='text-align:center'>Computer Science Question Paper</h1><p style='text-align:center'>Duration: 1 Hour | Total Marks: 100</p><hr/><p><b>Q1. Memory for objects in Java is allocated in:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Stack</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Register</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Heap</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Method area</div><br/><p><b>Q2. To organize classes, which statement is used at the top of a file?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) import</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) package</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) class</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) include</div><br/><p><b>Q3. Which of the following is NOT a tab in the 'CSS Stylesheets' dialog box?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Text</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Background</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Animation</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Aural</div><br/><p><b>Q4. Why does the POST method not have restrictions on data length compared to GET?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Because it uses a larger URL buffer.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Because data is sent as a block in the HTTP transaction, not in the URL.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Because it compresses the data.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Because it splits data into multiple GET requests.</div><br/><p><b>Q5. Easy: Which software tool is used for statistical computing and graphics?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) VLC</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) RationalPlan</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) R</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Skype</div><br/><p><b>Q6. What does the 'Split' view in KompoZer display?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Only the source code</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Only the design view</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Both the source code and the design view</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The browser preview</div><br/><p><b>Q7. Hard: In the Java `Date` class, the constructor `Date()` initializes the object with:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) January 1, 1970</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) A null value</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) The current system time</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The start of the program</div><br/><p><b>Q8. What symbol marks the end of the table in the compression example?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) $</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) %</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) &</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) @</div><br/><p><b>Q9. Hard: Which button allows you to add JavaScript events to a form element in KompoZer?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) More Properties</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Advanced Edit</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Define Script</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Add Event</div><br/><p><b>Q10. A package statement is used to:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Compile code</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Organize classes</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Hide classes</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Delete classes</div><br/><p><b>Q11. Which shortcut key is used to close the Site Manager pane in KompoZer?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) F5</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) F9</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Ctrl+S</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Esc</div><br/><p><b>Q12. Which button on the KompoZer Composition toolbar opens the CSS Stylesheets dialog?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Format</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Table</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Cascade</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Edit Mode</div><br/><p><b>Q13. What identifies an object and distinguishes it from others?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) State</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Behavior</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Identity</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Class</div><br/><p><b>Q14. Easy: In CSS syntax, the Property and Value are separated by which symbol?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Comma (,)</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Colon (:)</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Semicolon (;)</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Dash (-)</div><br/><p><b>Q15. A method defined with the 'static' keyword is called a:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Instance method</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Class method</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Constructor</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Local method</div><br/><p><b>Q16. Easy: Which HTML tag is used to create a multi-line text input area in a form?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) <input type='text'></div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) <textarea></div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) <textbox></div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) <edit></div><br/><p><b>Q17. Which version of RationalPlan is designed to manage independent projects?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) RationalPlan Multi</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) RationalPlan Single</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) RationalPlan Viewer</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) RationalPlan Solo</div><br/><p><b>Q18. Which constant in the Calendar class represents the day of the month?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) DAY</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) DATE</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) MONTH_DAY</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) DAY_NUM</div><br/><p><b>Q19. What is the Archive Manager used for?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Playing videos</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Drawing graphs</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Compressing and extracting files</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Writing documents</div><br/><p><b>Q20. What character starts a multi-line comment?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) //</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) /*</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) */</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) #</div><br/><p><b>Q21. Easy: Which of the following is a key advantage of M-Commerce mentioned in the text?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Larger screens</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Unlimited power supply</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Flexibility and Ubiquity</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) High-speed wired connection</div><br/><p><b>Q22. What happens if you try to access a member using a `null` reference?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) It works normally</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) It returns 0</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) It causes a runtime error (exception)</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) It creates a new object</div><br/><p><b>Q23. Which Java keyword is used to create a new object instance?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) class</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) object</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) new</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) instance</div><br/><p><b>Q24. Which subclass of Calendar is commonly used?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) GregorianCalendar</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) JulianCalendar</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) LunarCalendar</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) SolarCalendar</div><br/><p><b>Q25. Which tab allows you to set a background image for an element?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Box</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Text</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Background</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Lists</div><br/><p><b>Q26. Which button in the KompoZer Composition toolbar is used to open the CSS Stylesheets dialog box?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) The 'Form' button</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The 'Cascade' button</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) The 'Image' button</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The 'Save' button</div><br/><p><b>Q27. Which keyword is used to create a subclass in Java?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) inherits</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) extends</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) implements</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) super</div><br/><p><b>Q28. Skype is primarily used for?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Voice and video communication</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Drawing graphs</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Coding java</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Viewing maps</div><br/><p><b>Q29. Which concept defines a 'has-a' relationship?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Inheritance</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Aggregation/Composition</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Polymorphism</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Abstraction</div><br/><p><b>Q30. Which of the following cannot access instance variables directly?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Instance method</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Constructor</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Static method</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Object method</div><br/><p><b>Q31. Which type of variable is allocated memory from the 'Heap' area?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Local variables</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Instance variables</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Loop counters</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Method parameters</div><br/><p><b>Q32. In the CSS syntax, what follows the Selector?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) A value</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) A property</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) A declaration block enclosed in curly braces</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) A colon</div><br/><p><b>Q33. RationalPlan Viewer is specifically developed to open files from which proprietary software?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Adobe Photoshop</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Microsoft Project</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) AutoCAD</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Microsoft Excel</div><br/><p><b>Q34. Which operator assigns a value to a variable?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) ==</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) =</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) :</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) -></div><br/><p><b>Q35. What is the default value of a boolean variable?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) true</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) false</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) 0</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) null</div><br/><p><b>Q36. Which statement best describes the life cycle of a 'Local Variable'?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Created when object is created, destroyed when object is destroyed.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Created when method/block starts, destroyed when it ends.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Created when class is loaded, destroyed when program ends.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Created when main starts, destroyed when main ends.</div><br/><p><b>Q37. How do you allow a private variable to be modified by other classes safely?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Change it to public.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Use a 'Mutator' (setter) method.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Use a 'Getter' method.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Declare it as static.</div><br/><p><b>Q38. What does the `String` method `concat()` do in Java?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Removes whitespace</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Appends one string to the end of another</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Splits the string</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Compares two strings</div><br/><p><b>Q39. In the expression `x = y = z = 7`, in which order is the assignment performed?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Left to Right</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Right to Left</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Simultaneously</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Randomly</div><br/><p><b>Q40. In the 'Ten Little Indians' compression example, what was removed to save space?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Numbers</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Repetitive words</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Punctuation</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Spaces</div><br/><p><b>Q41. What is the default access modifier if no keyword is used?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) public</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) private</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) protected</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) package (default)</div><br/><p><b>Q42. When an object is passed as a parameter to a method, what is actually passed?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) A complete copy of the object</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The values of its attributes only</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) The address (reference) of the object</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The class definition</div><br/><p><b>Q43. In a constructor, `this` refers to:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) The superclass object</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The current object being initialized</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) The main method</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The class file</div><br/><p><b>Q44. Which event handler is used to call a validation function when a form is submitted?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) onclick</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) onchange</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) onsubmit</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) onload</div><br/><p><b>Q45. Which attribute of the `<textarea>` tag controls the visible width (number of characters) of the text area?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) width</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) size</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) cols</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) rows</div><br/><p><b>Q46. Which of the following constitutes a valid 'Method Signature' for overloading?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Method name and return type</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Method name and access modifier</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Method name and list of parameters (types/sequence)</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Method name and exception list</div><br/><p><b>Q47. If 'a = 12.5' (float) and 'b = 7.2' (float), why is 'a % b' equal to '5.3'?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) It is a truncation error.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The modulus operator works on floats in Java.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) It rounds to the nearest integer.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) It is a syntax error.</div><br/><p><b>Q48. What does the statement `return false` do in a form validation function?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Submits the form</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Stops the function and prevents form submission</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Refreshes the page</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Closes the browser</div><br/><p><b>Q49. What is the primary technical reason VLC can play almost any media format?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) It streams the data to a server.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) It has a modular design that supports all popular codecs natively.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) It converts all files to MP4 before playing.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) It uses the operating system's default players.</div><br/><p><b>Q50. What is the purpose of the 'main' method in a Java application?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) To declare variables.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) To define the class structure.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) It is the first routine run when the program executes.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) It compiles the code.</div><br/><p><b>Q51. Which button on the Composition Toolbar opens the CSS Stylesheets dialog box?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Image</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Table</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Cascade</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Form</div><br/><p><b>Q52. Which of these is NOT a visibility modifier symbol in UML?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) +</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) *</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) -</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) #</div><br/><p><b>Q53. Medium: To apply a style to all `h1` elements, which option do you select in the CSS dialog?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) style applied to all elements of class</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) style applied to all elements of type</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) style applied to an element with ID</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) custom style rule</div><br/><p><b>Q54. Easy: Which button creates a submit button in an HTML form?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) <input type='button'></div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) <input type='submit'></div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) <input type='reset'></div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) <input type='text'></div><br/><p><b>Q55. Easy: Which website is used as an example for 'Mobile Ticketing' in the text?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) eBay</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) IRCTC (Indian Railway Catering And Tourism Corporation)</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Amazon</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Google Maps</div><br/><p><b>Q56. An array variable is actually a:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Primitive type</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Reference variable</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Constant</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) String</div><br/><p><b>Q57. If you select 'internal stylesheet' in the CSS dialog, where is the CSS code physically stored?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) In an external .css file</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) In the <head> section of the HTML document</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Inline within HTML tags</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) In the browser's cache</div><br/><p><b>Q58. The Calendar constant `MONTH` uses 0 to represent which month?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) March</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) January</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) December</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) February</div><br/><p><b>Q59. What happens if you declare 'float rate = 10.2;' without a suffix?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) It compiles successfully.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) It rounds down to 10.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) It causes a compilation error.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) It converts it to an integer.</div><br/><p><b>Q60. What does `compareTo()` return if the invoking string is equal to the argument string?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) 1</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) -1</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) 0</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) true</div><br/><p><b>Q61. Medium: Which function in R is used to create a bar chart?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) hist()</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) plot()</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) barplot()</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) chart()</div><br/><p><b>Q62. How are multi-line comments denoted in Java?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) // ... //</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) /* ... */</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) </div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) # ... #</div><br/><p><b>Q63. Easy: Which tool allows you to compress files in Linux?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) VLC</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Archive Manager</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Character Map</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) R</div><br/><p><b>Q64. What does the expression `new Room()` return?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) The object itself</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The address of the memory location where the object is stored</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) A boolean value</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The size of the object</div><br/><p><b>Q65. The `package` statement in a Java source file must be:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Inside the class definition.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The first non-comment/non-blank line in the file.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) After the import statements.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Anywhere in the file.</div><br/><p><b>Q66. What is 'Method Overriding'?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Defining a new method with a different name</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Defining a method in subclass with the same signature as in superclass</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Overloading a method in the same class</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Deleting a method from the superclass</div><br/><p><b>Q67. To view a satellite image in Google Maps, what do you click?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) The Map button</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The Satellite button</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) The Earth button</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The View button</div><br/><p><b>Q68. What is the main limitation of RationalPlan Single compared to Multi?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) It cannot save files.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) It does not support common resources or inter-project links.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) It is not free.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) It only runs on Linux.</div><br/><p><b>Q69. In the 'Form Properties' dialog box, what value should be in the 'Action URL' field?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) The name of the form</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The HTTP method</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) The filename where data is sent</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The CSS file</div><br/><p><b>Q70. Medium: Which E-Commerce security aspect ensures that information is not accidentally or maliciously altered during transit?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Confidentiality</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Integrity</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Authorization</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Non-repudiation</div><br/><p><b>Q71. In JavaScript, `document.js1.name.value` is used to access data. What does `js1` represent?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) The name of the JavaScript file.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The name of the HTML document.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) The name of the Form element.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The name of the Submit button.</div><br/><p><b>Q72. When a file does not have a `package` statement, where are the classes placed?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) In the 'java.lang' package.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) In the 'default package'.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) They are not compiled.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) In the 'public' package.</div><br/><p><b>Q73. What happens when you declare a variable inside a block (between { })?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) It is global.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) It is visible everywhere.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) It ceases to exist after the block.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) It is promoted to the main method.</div><br/><p><b>Q74. Which logical operator represents AND?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) &</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) &&</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) AND</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) ||</div><br/><p><b>Q75. Hard: What does the JavaScript function `isNaN("123")` return?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) true</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) false</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) undefined</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) error</div><br/><p><b>Q76. If 'int a = 17' and 'short b', how must you assign 'a' to 'b'?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) b = a;</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) b = (short)a;</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) b = short(a);</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) b = a.toShort();</div><br/><p><b>Q77. Which tag creates a drop-down menu in an HTML form?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) <list></div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) <select></div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) <dropdown></div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) <option></div><br/><p><b>Q78. What does the `main` argument in the R `barplot` function specify?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) The main color</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The main dataset</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) The main title of the graph</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The main axis</div><br/><p><b>Q79. Which command is used to execute a Java application?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) javac</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) start</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) execute</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) java</div><br/><p><b>Q80. Hard: What specific value does the `<form>` attribute `action` expect?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) A boolean (true/false)</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) A filename or URL</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) A method type (GET/POST)</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) A CSS style</div><br/><p><b>Q81. Static methods belong to:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Objects</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Constructors</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Class</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Heap memory</div><br/><p><b>Q82. Which notation uses dot (.) to access members?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Object notation</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Dot operator</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Arrow operator</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Colon operator</div><br/><p><b>Q83. How can you close the Site Manager pane in KompoZer?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Press F5</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Press F9</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Press F12</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Press Esc</div><br/><p><b>Q84. Medium: Information Services in E-Commerce allow users to:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Buy physical goods only</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Access educational results, notices, and forms online</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Chat with friends</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Edit videos</div><br/><p><b>Q85. How does Skype charge for calls to traditional landline telephones?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) It is free.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) It uses a debit-based user account system.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) It uses a monthly subscription only.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) It charges the receiver.</div><br/><p><b>Q86. Medium: What does the `return false;` statement do in a form validation script?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Submits the form</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Prevents the form from being submitted</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Reloads the page</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Validates the data</div><br/><p><b>Q87. According to the text, RationalPlan Multi is specifically distinguished from RationalPlan Single by its ability to manage:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Large budgets.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Common resources across interdependent projects.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Only .pdf files.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Cloud-based storage.</div><br/><p><b>Q88. In the R code `hist(marks, col="lightblue")`, what data type must `marks` be?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) A single integer.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) A string.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) A vector/list of numerical values.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) A function.</div><br/><p><b>Q89. If `Classroom` extends `Room`, and you want to use the `display()` method of `Room` inside `Classroom`'s overriding `display()` method, how do you write it?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Room.display();</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) this.display();</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) super.display();</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) display();</div><br/><p><b>Q90. Medium: In the Java code `int marks[][] = new int[5][3];`, how many total integers can be stored in the array `marks`?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) 8</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) 15</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) 53</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) 2</div><br/><p><b>Q91. Which tab in the CSS dialog displays the generated CSS code?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Text</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) General</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Aural</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Box</div><br/><p><b>Q92. Medium: Which Free Tool is used for statistical computing?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) VLC</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) RationalPlan</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) R</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Skype</div><br/><p><b>Q93. Scientific notation 1.3e12 represents:</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) 1.3 * 10^12</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) 1.3 * 12</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) 1.3 + 12</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) 13^12</div><br/><p><b>Q94. Hard: In Java, what is the index of the last element in an array of size `n`?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) n</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) n - 1</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) n + 1</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) 0</div><br/><p><b>Q95. Hard: Where should the `<script>` tag ideally be placed in an HTML document?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Inside the <title> tag</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Inside the <head> or <body> tag</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Only after the </html> tag</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Inside the CSS file</div><br/><p><b>Q96. In the R command `barplot`, what does the `xlab` argument specify?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) The title of the graph</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) The label for the Y-axis</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) The label for the X-axis</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) The color of the bars</div><br/><p><b>Q97. What color were the bars in the R example graph?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) Red</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) Blue</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) Green</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) Yellow</div><br/><p><b>Q98. Hard: What specifically happens to the default constructor in a Java class if you define a parameterized constructor?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) It remains available.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) It is no longer available and must be explicitly defined if needed.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) It becomes private.</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) It creates a compilation error immediately.</div><br/><p><b>Q99. What is the decimal value of the hexadecimal literal '0x10'?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) 10</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) 16</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) 12</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) 20</div><br/><p><b>Q100. Which command compiles a Java program?</b></p><div style='margin-left:20px'>a) java</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>b) javac</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>c) run</div><div style='margin-left:20px'>d) compile</div><br/><br/><hr/><h1 style='text-align:center'>Answer Key</h1><p>1. (c) Heap</p><p>2. (b) package</p><p>3. (c) Animation</p><p>4. (b) Because data is sent as a block in the HTTP transaction, not in the URL.</p><p>5. (c) R</p><p>6. (c) Both the source code and the design view</p><p>7. (c) The current system time</p><p>8. (a) $</p><p>9. (b) Advanced Edit</p><p>10. (b) Organize classes</p><p>11. (b) F9</p><p>12. (c) Cascade</p><p>13. (c) Identity</p><p>14. (b) Colon (:)</p><p>15. (b) Class method</p><p>16. (b) <textarea></p><p>17. (b) RationalPlan Single</p><p>18. (b) DATE</p><p>19. (c) Compressing and extracting files</p><p>20. (b) /*</p><p>21. (c) Flexibility and Ubiquity</p><p>22. (c) It causes a runtime error (exception)</p><p>23. (c) new</p><p>24. (a) GregorianCalendar</p><p>25. (c) Background</p><p>26. (b) The 'Cascade' button</p><p>27. (b) extends</p><p>28. (a) Voice and video communication</p><p>29. (b) Aggregation/Composition</p><p>30. (c) Static method</p><p>31. (b) Instance variables</p><p>32. (c) A declaration block enclosed in curly braces</p><p>33. (b) Microsoft Project</p><p>34. (b) =</p><p>35. (b) false</p><p>36. (b) Created when method/block starts, destroyed when it ends.</p><p>37. (b) Use a 'Mutator' (setter) method.</p><p>38. (b) Appends one string to the end of another</p><p>39. (b) Right to Left</p><p>40. (b) Repetitive words</p><p>41. (d) package (default)</p><p>42. (c) The address (reference) of the object</p><p>43. (b) The current object being initialized</p><p>44. (c) onsubmit</p><p>45. (c) cols</p><p>46. (c) Method name and list of parameters (types/sequence)</p><p>47. (b) The modulus operator works on floats in Java.</p><p>48. (b) Stops the function and prevents form submission</p><p>49. (b) It has a modular design that supports all popular codecs natively.</p><p>50. (c) It is the first routine run when the program executes.</p><p>51. (c) Cascade</p><p>52. (b) *</p><p>53. (b) style applied to all elements of type</p><p>54. (b) <input type='submit'></p><p>55. (b) IRCTC (Indian Railway Catering And Tourism Corporation)</p><p>56. (b) Reference variable</p><p>57. (b) In the <head> section of the HTML document</p><p>58. (b) January</p><p>59. (c) It causes a compilation error.</p><p>60. (c) 0</p><p>61. (c) barplot()</p><p>62. (b) /* ... */</p><p>63. (b) Archive Manager</p><p>64. (b) The address of the memory location where the object is stored</p><p>65. (b) The first non-comment/non-blank line in the file.</p><p>66. (b) Defining a method in subclass with the same signature as in superclass</p><p>67. (b) The Satellite button</p><p>68. (b) It does not support common resources or inter-project links.</p><p>69. (c) The filename where data is sent</p><p>70. (b) Integrity</p><p>71. (c) The name of the Form element.</p><p>72. (b) In the 'default package'.</p><p>73. (c) It ceases to exist after the block.</p><p>74. (b) &&</p><p>75. (b) false</p><p>76. (b) b = (short)a;</p><p>77. (b) <select></p><p>78. (c) The main title of the graph</p><p>79. (d) java</p><p>80. (b) A filename or URL</p><p>81. (c) Class</p><p>82. (b) Dot operator</p><p>83. (b) Press F9</p><p>84. (b) Access educational results, notices, and forms online</p><p>85. (b) It uses a debit-based user account system.</p><p>86. (b) Prevents the form from being submitted</p><p>87. (b) Common resources across interdependent projects.</p><p>88. (c) A vector/list of numerical values.</p><p>89. (c) super.display();</p><p>90. (b) 15</p><p>91. (b) General</p><p>92. (c) R</p><p>93. (a) 1.3 * 10^12</p><p>94. (b) n - 1</p><p>95. (b) Inside the <head> or <body> tag</p><p>96. (c) The label for the X-axis</p><p>97. (b) Blue</p><p>98. (b) It is no longer available and must be explicitly defined if needed.</p><p>99. (b) 16</p><p>100. (b) javac</p></body></html>